  "dataQualityNote": "4 of 24 arm samples were StructuredOutput artifacts (a \"test\" echo / zero-quality), 2 per arm \u2014 symmetric noise, small n. Discounting them does not flip the sign.",
  "verdict": "Within noise under retrieval misses \u2014 aot verification/refine does not reliably beat a capable model's own re-search on this suite.",
  "finding": "NO BENEFIT DEMONSTRATED (not \"falsified\" \u2014 a within-noise null at n=4 with 17% corrupted samples fails to CONFIRM aot value; it cannot falsify). Overall margin -0.100 < noise 0.127 (clears:false). Correct-grounding aot 9/12 vs baseline 10/12 \u2014 a ONE-sample difference, i.e. noise, not a directional signal. No reliable aot benefit shown even in its predicted retrieval-miss regime, at this scale.",
  "narrowPocketOfValue": "SUGGESTIVE (not established): on the single most severe decoy (adv-dead-letter, letter/message -> outlook-email), aot scored +0.123 with correct-grounding 3/3 vs 2/3. Consistent with the judge --refutes + refine mechanism, but n=1 task with 3 replicates \u2014 too small to confirm. A pocket worth a larger-n follow-up, not a demonstrated win.",
  "conclusion": "Across run-002 (textbook -0.084, decisive), run-integration-v2 (uncontaminated retrieval -0.142, decisive), and run-adversarial (retrieval-miss -0.100, WITHIN NOISE / unconfirmed), the aot epistemic layer shows no reliable benefit over raw sgt + a capable model \u2014 including in its predicted best regime. One suggestive win (dead-letter) is too small to confirm. Engineering conclusion holds: keep raw sgt retrieval as default; a larger adversarial suite is a user-authorized follow-up, not a determined result.",
  "powerCaveat": "UNDERPOWERED: n=4 tasks, k=3, and 4/24 samples were StructuredOutput artifacts (2 per arm). Conclusions are \"no benefit demonstrated at this scale\", NOT \"benefit disproven\"."
